				<h3 class="cm-kicker cm-kicker--plain" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-3)">head title hook</h3>
				<p class="cm-head__sub" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-3)">
					<code>.cm-head h1</code> already sizes the title, so
					<code>.cm-head__title</code> is the hook for a title
					that is not an <code>h1</code> &mdash; an
					<code>aria-label</code> on a landmark, or a
					<code>&lt;h2&gt;</code> leading a section. It reads
					the same size either way, which is the point: the
					selector is a pair, not two competing rules.
				</p>
				<div class="cm-head" style="padding:0">
